#
# OCI 11.2's `declare o pyo_obj_t := :1; begin :2 := o.n || ':' || o.s; end;`
# binding PYO.PYO_OBJ_T (n NUMBER, s VARCHAR2(20)) as (42, 'hello') IN (#2463):
# the object's descriptor an ADT (109) of 2000 bytes, the type's 16-byte OID
# 5fb718dacaedebe5e060a8c096004fdb and version 1, flags 0; its value the native
# object cell, the constructed 36-byte toid, the TOP_LEVEL flags and the packed
# image; then the VARCHAR2 OUT bind's descriptor and its empty value.
# Captured 2026-11-07 through tools/capture_proxy.py: an OCI 11.2 program
# (instant client 11.2, x86-64 Linux, the client charset AL32UTF8, the object
# cache on; OCITypeByName, OCIObjectNew and OCIObjectSetAttr, then OCIBindObject
# of an SQLT_NTY bind, called through ctypes) on Oracle 11g XE 11.2.0.2, a
# DEDICATED session, with a throwaway type dropped after. The TTC payload,
# without the packet's header, as `hexdump -C` output; the offset column and the
# |ascii| gutter are ignored by tests.replay.parse_hexdump.
